    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Let me create a final summary:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Issue:** `frai gate init --ci` was not creating `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` because the `--ci` flag was not being passed through from the frai CLI to frai-gate.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `gate` command action callback in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (line 742) only captured positional arguments (`args: string[]`), while flags like `--ci` were being lost.\n\n**Solution:** Modified the action callback to extract all arguments after 'gate' from `process.argv` and pass them to frai-gate, ensuring both positional arguments and flags are properly forwarded.\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- **File:** `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-754)\n- Added: Extract `gateIndex` and `gateArgs` from `process.argv`\n- Changed: Pass `gateArgs` instead of just `args` to `spawnSync`\n\n**Testing:**\n\u2705 Test 1: `frai gate init --ci` \u2192 Creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\u2705 Test 2: `frai gate init --ci --out TEST-SPEC.md` \u2192 Creates `TEST-SPEC.md` and workflow, respecting both flags\n\nAll tasks completed successfully!",
